# GitHub releases

When creating or editing a GitHub release (`gh release create` / `gh release edit`):

- Notes are a one-line intro, then a **markdown bullet list** (one change per bullet). Never a paragraph of semicolon-joined sentences.
- Do not put a download link in the notes. The Assets list is enough.
- Upload **one** app zip, named `Audiochrome.zip` (copy of the notarized `Audiochrome-<version>.zip`). Do not also attach the versioned filename.
- Leave GitHub’s source archives as-is.
- After a versioned release, update the README download line to `Download Audiochrome (X.Y.Z version history)` — Download Audiochrome → `releases/latest/download/Audiochrome.zip`, X.Y.Z version history → `releases`.

```markdown
Signed and notarized macOS build.

- EQ editor groups filters by Both / Left / Right channel
- Available EQs and Effects open when nothing is selected
- Other Devices and an open device stay exclusive
```
